<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran's nuclear program remains shrouded in mystery as the regime debates ditching non-proliferation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99c54e810542b6321bdccfabccda4a27c4237d5bc5e43ef3dd2efe8f8be1e94e</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197--eb083345c8e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's nuclear program is entering a critical phase as Tehran debates dropping out of a nuclear non-proliferation treaty. Satellite images also show activity at known nuclear sites.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Fullbright scholar imprisoned for 13 years in a Pakistani jail, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abb79f23a08ff0d37d5aaf3ff596efc5111e508ae85fcb314f0fa1edad06b3b0</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-fullbright-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-in-a-pakistani-jail-is-hope/a-79490207--2eb272f62665.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-fullbright-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-in-a-pakistani-jail-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fullbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia elections: Polls overshadowed by exhaustion, exodus and geopolitics as ethnic politics eclipse real problems</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77285c26a0419e10ce6ddadc0c0e8f1f39f1ad78c4c9f0dbbdca7c9c596e7f69</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-/a-79487802--91e658c381f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-real-problems/a-79487802?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia goes to the polls on October 4 to elect several parliaments and presidents. While voters worry about the economy and emigration, the campaign is focused on ethnicity, exposing the country's political paralysis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7857503838d074e4a2858e4806c04ebcf097435e87dcfebd6097a36a378e9471</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Eurovision remains marred by geopolitics: Ireland will boycott again because of Israel's participation. Still, the song contest is expanding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba8898ff95b4e37da6e4e1678214e861db0f7f9bd38f63b576ca659b26735726</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eurovision-remains-marred-by-geopolitics-ireland-will-boycott-again-because-of-israel-s-participatio/a-79401752--b320a0475ab7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eurovision-remains-marred-by-geopolitics-ireland-will-boycott-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-still-the-song-contest-is-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea: Lost shark draws over half a million visitors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4315dda5eabe3c364494e66cbd64a75c2e92517d9ced5dcfb0cb84e3c3cfe92b</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014--618815d2f667.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The South Korean port of Busan says that a stranded shark has become a major tourist draw. It's also named the ocean predator an honorary ambassador to the city.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Alternative Nobel' honors women's rights activists, AI researcher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebbd73386f441d1da028762280bfcbb0e97f087954336df91d39a95f66c7515a</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alternative-nobel-honors-women-s-rights-activists-ai-researcher/a-79481171--13d01235661c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alternative-nobel-honors-women-s-rights-activists-ai-researcher/a-79481171?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Right Livelihood Award has gone to a female AI researcher and women fighting repression. The Sweden-based prize has been dubbed an "alternative Nobel."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary's reckoning with Orban's corrupt system picks up speed with high-profile arrests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9333094e7094c43735b6c12b200f2a14c9ffc1fec9fce342af1957e0ea9cd5c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed-with-high-profile-arrests/a-79473714--21394904d7e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed-with-high-profile-arrests/a-79473714?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's Prime Minister Peter Magyar vowed to dismantle Orban's corrupt networks. High-profile figures are being arrested and many Hungarians are pushing for swift accountability, but the rule of law takes time.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: No regard for civilians as fighting in Ethiopia's Tigray region continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c670622b07e066a14cb4c1c258717cbc3755ab4de2da408741233f38267417c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-no-regard-for-civilians-as-fighting-in-ethiopia-s-tigray-region-continues/a-79464569--b348a7925ac4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-no-regard-for-civilians-as-fighting-in-ethiopia-s-tigray-region-continues/a-79464569?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fighting has returned to northern Ethiopia, shattering a fragile peace in the region. DW spoke to civilians caught in the crossfire amid communication blackouts, as rebel and federal forces keep battling for territory.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham seeks 'hope again' at Labour Party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14202bd67bcc136c7cf573e4d119f4981c8dd9ef43dd2f5fe84964a486b1e560</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376--71e603fc9e60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham is seeking a delicate balance between optimism and realism at Labour's annual party conference. He promised hope and an end to "politics as usual" but also an "honest conversation" about difficult dilemmas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01ad9355d1ad254cbc3e276d2510a4c6fb9fecf74fba29cdbf94d4e36e0dedfb</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women and children displaced by Nepal's floods say safe housing, privacy and stability remain out of reach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8fe5aea548be2b2a95dd11960e225d91931ea9a613a0dc55091384d161f8a7f</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-/a-79474014--5ad51afec87b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-reach/a-79474014?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Families living in temporary shelters in northern Nepal say safety and privacy remain out of reach as concerns about trafficking and abuse mount.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
